  "operative_text": "Section 1 (new section in SDCL ch. 34-20G): A dispensary shall post, at each entrance used by the public and at each cash register or point of sale, a conspicuous sign that: (1) Is clearly visible to an individual, whether sitting or standing; and (2) Contains the following words: WARNING: Federal law prohibits the possession of a firearm by certain individuals who are users of or addicted to marijuana. See 18 U.S.C. § 922(g) (January 1, 2024). Except as otherwise provided, a dispensary that violates this section is subject to a civil penalty in the amount of two hundred and fifty dollars per day.\nSection 2 (uncodified): The department shall cease to enforce the requirements set forth in section 1 of this Act upon receiving a certification from the Attorney General indicating that federal law no longer prohibits the possession of a firearm by certain individuals who are users of or addicted to marijuana."
}